    "about": "Strata Markets is a structured yield protocol on Ethereum that splits yield-bearing asset returns into Senior and Junior tranches, each implemented as ERC-4626 meta-vaults. Users deposit assets such as USDe, NUSD, mHYPER, mM1-USD, or USDat and receive either a senior tranche token (lower risk, moderate return) or a junior tranche token (higher risk, higher potential return). The protocol's dynamic yield-split mechanism routes collateral returns between tranches based on real-time APR data sourced from on-chain feeds. Admin actions are governed by a 3-of-4 multisig, a 2-of-3 operational multisig, 48-hour and 24-hour timelocks, and an external Guardian (Cyfrin co-founder) with veto power over queued timelock transactions."
